{
  "opening": "The boltons library is releasing version 19.1.0, which introduces several enhancements to its utility modules. The glom project depends on boltons and must adopt these changes to ensure compatibility and access new features.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "In the boltons library, the OneToOne class and FastIterOrderedMultiDict must correctly handle inputs where keys map to multiple values without raising errors or losing data. The unique function should return a collection preserving the order of first occurrence for non-unique items."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "In the boltons library, FunctionBuilder.get_arg_names must return all argument names including keyword-only arguments. FunctionBuilder.get_defaults_dict must include defaults for keyword-only arguments, and inspect_formatargspec must format arguments with annotations when available."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12c",
      "text": "When using glom, the underlying boltons FunctionBuilder.get_arg_names method must expose keyword-only argument names in its output. The get_defaults_dict method from boltons must include defaults for keyword-only arguments as observed through glom's internal usage."
    },
    {
      "id": "m19",
      "text": "In the boltons library, the ComplementSet class must support the __rsub__ operator, allowing subtraction operations where the set is on the right side of the operator. The difference_update method must correctly update the set by removing elements found in another iterable."
    },
    {
      "id": "m22",
      "text": "In the glom library, the Glommer class and top-level functions like glom, glomit, first, flatten, filter, chunked, dropwhile, and fill must operate correctly with the updated boltons dependencies. Spec types such as Auto, Check, Fill, First, Iter, Let, TType, and Inspect must maintain their existing behavior for data transformation and validation."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure that all public APIs mentioned above behave as described in this release. These changes are critical for maintaining stability between boltons and glom."
}
